  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In a common emitter amplifier circuit, the input voltage must be forward biased and output voltage must be reversed biased.</p><p>So the&nbsp;input voltage must be out of phase of output voltage.</p>Therefore, the phase difference between the input and output voltage is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.",
